  <front>
    <title>RFC 3627 to Historic Status</title>
    <seriesInfo name="RFC" value="6547" stream="IETF"/>
    <date year="2012" month="February"/>
    <abstract pn="section-abstract">
      <t indent="0" pn="section-abstract-1">This document moves &quot;Use of /127 Prefix Length Between Routers
Considered Harmful&quot; (RFC 3627) to Historic status to reflect the
updated guidance contained in &quot;Using 127-Bit IPv6 Prefixes on Inter-Router Links&quot; (RFC 6164).  A Standards Track document supersedes an
informational document; therefore, guidance provided in RFC 6164 is
to be followed when the two documents are in conflict.  This document
links the two RFCs so that the IETF's updated guidance on this topic
is clearer.</t>
    </abstract>
