  <middle>
    <section anchor="introduction" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-1">
      <name slugifiedName="name-introduction">Introduction</name>
      <t indent="0" pn="section-1-1">This document moves &quot;Use of /127 Prefix Length Between Routers
Considered Harmful&quot; <xref target="RFC3627" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC3627"/> to Historic status in accordance with
RFC 2026 <xref target="RFC2026" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC2026"/>.  RFC 3627 has been superseded by &quot;Using 127-Bit
IPv6 Prefixes on Inter-Router Links&quot; <xref target="RFC6164" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="RFC6164"/>.  A Standards Track
document supersedes an informational document; therefore, guidance
provided in RFC 6164 is to be followed when the two documents are in
conflict.  This may not have been clear to casual readers who are not
familiar with the differences in IETF document types.  This document
adds the necessary link between the two RFCs so that users referring
to RFC 3627 for guidance will see that it has been obsoleted by
updated guidance on the matter, thus hopefully eliminating any
confusion that may be present.</t>
    </section>
